   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<p><img src=\"exercises/media/102227f6533a0f3f.jpg\" alt=\"A Punnett square shows the heterozygous parents of four possible genotypes. The offspring genotypes shown are 1 homozygous for smooth seeds, 2 heterozygous, and 1 missing.\"></p>\n\n<p>In pea plants, smooth seeds (S) are dominant to wrinkled seeds (s). In a genetic cross of two plants that are heterozygous for the seed shape trait, the Punnett square is shown. What is the missing genotype?</p>\n",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 722165,
     "content_html": "SS"
    },
    {
     "id": 722164,
     "content_html": "Ss"
    },
    {
